course: dictionary
lesson: 10260
title: Tonsillitis and the body
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Tonsillitis is a long word, so break it into parts. Tonsil is the first part, and -itis at the end often means swelling or soreness in a part of the body. The tonsils are two lumps of soft tissue at the back of your throat. So tonsillitis means the tonsils are infected and swollen.
explain: The sentence gives you clues: «Tonsils are lumps at the back of the throat that help fight germs» tells you where they are and what they do. Then «a few bouts of tonsillitis (sore, swollen tonsils)» explains the word in brackets. Brackets often give you a meaning straight away.
explain: Notice «a bout of tonsillitis». A bout is one spell of an illness, so a few bouts means a few separate times someone has been ill with it. Tonsillitis is not counted like apples, so you say «have tonsillitis», never «two tonsillitises».
fact: Tonsillitis means the tonsils at the back of the throat become infected and swollen.
fact: It causes a sore throat, pain when swallowing and often a fever.
fact: Most cases are caused by a virus; sometimes bacteria, such as strep, cause it.
fact: Rest, drinks and painkillers from an adult help; a doctor may give antibiotics if it is bacterial.
fact: A tonsillectomy is an operation to remove the tonsils, and it is only done for children who get tonsillitis very often.
exercise: Where are the tonsils? | On the top of the head | On the foot | *At the back of the throat | In the stomach
exercise: Priya has tonsillitis and her throat hurts when she swallows. Which symptom is she describing? | *Pain when swallowing | A runny nose only | A cut knee | Itchy eyes
exercise: Why might a doctor give antibiotics for tonsillitis? | Because the tonsils are too small | To make the tonsils bigger | *Because the tonsillitis is caused by bacteria | Because a broken bone needs them
test: In «a bout of tonsillitis», what does bout mean? | A bottle of medicine | *A single spell of an illness | A visit to the dentist | A kind of throat sweet
test: What is a tonsillectomy? | *An operation to remove the tonsils | A drink to soothe the throat | A cough medicine | A test for sore throats
exam: The sentence «a few bouts of tonsillitis are not a reason to take them out» tells you that | Tonsillitis always needs an operation | Tonsils are useless and can be ignored | Tonsils are found in the stomach | *A few bouts of tonsillitis are not enough reason for an operation
